    "question": "When should I use Docker containers instead of a virtual machine, and what is the real difference?",
    "summary": "Docker containers and virtual machines both isolate applications but differ fundamentally: containers share the host OS kernel for lightweight, fast deployments, while VMs emulate full hardware for stronger isolation. Containers excel in cloud-native and microservices scenarios; VMs are preferred…",
